(7701164, 1264041, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment:<br/> <br/>The bends and curves in the road are the lines that guide the eye to travel and explore the beauty of this rural landscape. The forest and the blue sky with fluffy clouds add to the appeal  this is the beginning of a scenic roadtrip.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment: The bends and curves in the road are the lines that guide the eye to travel and explore the beauty of this rural landscape. The forest and the blue sky with fluffy clouds add to the appeal  this is the beginning of a scenic roadtrip.', '2021-09-12 22:00:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(7701165, 1264113, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment:<br/> <br/>A very pastoral and scenic commute that is definitely the less stressway to travel. No honking horns only the occasional bleeting of sheep:-) Love the view of the mountains in the distance!</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment: A very pastoral and scenic commute that is definitely the less stressway to travel. No honking horns only the occasional bleeting of sheep:-) Love the view of the mountains in the distance!', '2021-09-12 22:00:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(7701166, 1263813, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment:<br/> <br/>Love the title for it plays on a couple of interpretations. It can tie into the driving emotion that some get a day or two before travel; excitement, nervousness, anticipation to get started and hit the road. It also calls attention the swerving skid marks on the road  perhaps the driver of the car is a little too excited that they cant contain their boundless energy - which is visible by the marks they leave behind on the road. OR, or it could be that the anticipation alludes to that of the driver/us that sees this crazy driver in front of us weaving in and out ahead. In this interpretation, the wise choice is to take the foot off the accelerator to slow down and give them a wide berth.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment: Love the title for it plays on a couple of interpretations. It can tie into the driving emotion that some get a day or two before travel; excitement, nervousness, anticipation to get started and hit the road. It also calls attention the swerving skid marks on the road  perhaps the driver of the car is a little too excited that they cant contain their boundless energy - which is visible by the marks they leave behind on the road. OR, or it could be that the anticipation alludes to that of the driver/us that sees this crazy driver in front of us weaving in and out ahead. In this interpretation, the wise choice is to take the foot off the accelerator to slow down and give them a wide berth.', '2021-09-12 22:03:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(7701167, 1264107, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment:<br/> <br/>A person kneels down on the middle of the road to capture the moment that speaks of the taking the path leading to off to adventure and exploration of the mountains beyond. As an observer I feel the invitation to travel, to see, to explore with your capture of another photographer capturing that spirit of travel  the road trip to see and discover the beauty of the land. Nicely captured!</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment: A person kneels down on the middle of the road to capture the moment that speaks of the taking the path leading to off to adventure and exploration of the mountains beyond. As an observer I feel the invitation to travel, to see, to explore with your capture of another photographer capturing that spirit of travel  the road trip to see and discover the beauty of the land. Nicely captured!', '2021-09-12 22:04:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(7701213, 1264099, 101668, '<td valign="top">Western Cape! Beautiful</td>', 'Western Cape! Beautiful', '2021-09-13 08:08:27.000000', NULL, 1),
